{
    "background_story": "Tessa was a brilliant astronaut and engineer who played a crucial role in the development of the orbital space station, Aurora. Her expertise lay in designing modular systems that could be easily integrated and upgraded. Tessa's innovative approach allowed the station to be expanded and reconfigured as needed, making it a versatile hub for scientific research and exploration. One of her most notable contributions was the creation of the 'Tessa Module', a self-sustaining unit that could be attached to the station, providing additional living quarters, life support systems, and laboratory space. The module became a standard component of the Aurora's architecture, and Tessa's work paved the way for future space missions, earning her the nickname 'The Module Maven'.",
